\v 32 But¦115790 I'd¦115789 like you¦115791 to¦115793 be¦115793 free from concern. Single¦115795 men are¦115796 concerned¦115796 about things of¦115798 the¦115798 \nd master¦115799\nd*—pleasing¦115801 the¦115803 \nd master¦115804\nd*—
\v 33 but¦115806 married¦115807 men are¦115808 concerned¦115808 about¦115810 worldly¦115811 affairs—wanting to¦115815 please¦115813 \add &their¦115815\add* \add #wives¦115816\add*—so¦115817 they're divided¦115818. And unmarried¦115823 or single \add #women¦115821\add*
\v 34 are¦115829 concerning about things of¦115831 the¦115831 \nd master¦115832\nd*—so that¦115833 both¦115836 \add &their¦115837\add* \add #bodies¦115838\add* and¦115839 \add &their¦115840\add* \add #spirits¦115841\add* can be separate \add from the world\add*—but¦115843 married¦115844 women¦115842 are¦115845 concerned¦115845 about¦115847 worldly¦115848 affairs—wanting to¦115852 please¦115850 \add &their¦115852\add* \add #husbands¦115853\add*.
\p
\v 35 Now I¦115862 said¦115862 \add all\add* that¦115854 for¦115856 your¦115858 benefit¦115860—not¦115863 to load you¦115866 all¦115866 with rules, but¦115868 to \add act\add* in ways that are¦115870 appropriate and¦115872 devoted¦115873 to¦115875 the¦115875 \nd master¦115876\nd* without any distractions.
\p
\v 36 However, if¦115880 a man thinks¦115888 he's made the¦115885 wrong decisions about his¦115887 unmarried woman,\f + \fr 7:36-38 \ft Yes, ‘his unmarried woman’ sounds strange, but it's not certain here (and in the next two verses) if Paul is writing about a father and \+em his unmarried daughter who's engaged\+em*, or about an engaged man deciding about \+em his fiancée\+em*.\f* if¦115889 she's¦115890 reached the age¦115892 of marriage¦115892 and¦115893 it¦115896 should¦115896 proceed, then he¦115899 should¦115900 do¦115900 what¦115898 he planned—he's not¦115901 sinning¦115902—they should¦115903 get¦115897 married¦115903.
\v 37 But¦115905 if the man has made up his¦115911 \add ≈mind\add* and isn't¦115913 forced, but¦115917 makes his¦115920 own¦115921 decision, and¦115923 he's¦115904 firmly¦115912 decided to¦115932 keep¦115932 his¦115927 own¦115928 woman unmarried, then that¦115924 would¦115937 also be¦115937 a good decision.
